From: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:30:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: spi-nor: eon: enable dual read for en25qh32

The EN25QH32B on the TP-Link XZ000-G7 identifies as 1c:70:16. Its
datasheet specifies Dual Output Fast Read (3Bh) with eight dummy clocks
and an SFDP table. This is a different part from EN25Q32B (1c:30:16).

The fixed-size en25qh32 entry takes the legacy parameter path. Declare
dual read so that path supports 1-1-2 reads and attempts SFDP parsing,
falling back to the datasheet's 3Bh timing if parsing fails. The board
device tree advertises two data lines and keeps the SPI clock at 50 MHz.

Signed-off-by: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/mtd/spi-nor/eon.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/eon.c b/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/eon.c
--- a/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/eon.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/eon.c
@@ -51,6 +51,7 @@ static const struct flash_info eon_nor_parts[] = {
 		.id = SNOR_ID(0x1c, 0x70, 0x16),
 		.name = "en25qh32",
 		.size = SZ_4M,
+		.no_sfdp_flags = SPI_NOR_DUAL_READ,
 	}, {
 		.id = SNOR_ID(0x1c, 0x70, 0x17),
 		.name = "en25qh64",
-- 
2.46.1
